The error ORA-12899: value too large for column "FINCORE"."COMMON_REQ"."CHANGE_TYPE" (actual: 3, maximum: 2) happens because your Java code is trying to insert the full word "ADD" (3 letters) into the database, but the shared database column CHANGE_TYPE only allows 2 characters.
This confirms that the existing COMMON_REQ table uses Single Character Codes (like 'A' for ADD, 'U' for UPDATE) instead of full words.
To fix this, we must map your Enums to these short codes using a Converter, exactly like the reference architecture.
Here are the 4 Updated/New Files you need to fix this.
1. Update ChangeType Enum
Add the database code field ("A", "U", etc.).
File: src/main/java/com/fincore/YearEndService/Model/ChangeType.java
package com.fincore.YearEndService.Model;

import lombok.Getter;

@Getter
public enum ChangeType {
    ADD("A"),
    UPDATE("U"),
    DELETE("D");

    private final String code;

    ChangeType(String code) {
        this.code = code;
    }
}

2. Create ChangeTypeConverter
This tells JPA: "When saving ChangeType.ADD, write 'A' to the database."
File: src/main/java/com/fincore/YearEndService/Model/Converter/ChangeTypeConverter.java
package com.fincore.YearEndService.Model.Converter;

import com.fincore.YearEndService.Model.ChangeType;
import jakarta.persistence.AttributeConverter;
import jakarta.persistence.Converter;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

@Converter(autoApply = true)
public class ChangeTypeConverter implements AttributeConverter<ChangeType, String> {

    @Override
    public String convertToDatabaseColumn(ChangeType changeType) {
        if (changeType == null) return null;
        return changeType.getCode(); // Returns "A" instead of "ADD"
    }

    @Override
    public ChangeType convertToEntityAttribute(String code) {
        if (code == null) return null;
        return Stream.of(ChangeType.values())
                .filter(c -> c.getCode().equals(code))
                .findFirst()
                .orElseThrow(IllegalArgumentException::new);
    }
}

